{"content": "# Member newsletter blurb

**Your association filed on the Great American AI Act. Here's what we said.**

On Oct. 23 ACIA submitted comments to Reps. Jay Obernolte (R-Calif.) and Lori Trahan (D-Mass.) on the discussion draft of the Great American Artificial Intelligence Act. We backed the bill's core: one national standard for AI development, with preemption of state development rules made permanent rather than set to expire in three years. We opposed incident reporting as drafted, asking for a narrow definition of "critical safety incident," a locked-in 15-day window matching California rather than New York's 72 hours, a FOIA exemption for reports and a good-faith safe harbor for reporters. We backed codifying CAISI on a voluntary footing and opposed any mandatory pre-deployment testing gate. Throughout, we led with your numbers: 34% of startup members delayed a launch in California or New York last year, and frontier developers spend a median 6.5 full-time staff on parallel state compliance. Questions on the filing go to Tessa Marchetti.", "path": "/workspace/out/newsletter_blurb.md"}
